Spring Boot Basics Notes
What is Spring Boot?

Spring Boot is a framework built on top of the Spring Framework. It helps developers build production-ready Java applications with minimal configuration.

Spring Container

The Spring Container is responsible for:

Creating objects (Beans)
Managing their lifecycle
Injecting dependencies automatically
Spring Bean

A Spring Bean is an object created and managed by the Spring Container.

Example:

@Service
public class BookService {

}

**Dependency Injection (DI)**

Dependency Injection is a design pattern where a class receives
its dependencies from the outside instead of creating them itself.


**Constructor Injection**

Constructor Injection provides all required dependencies when an object is created.

It is the recommended way in Spring Boot because dependencies are mandatory and can be declared as final.


**Setter Injection**

Setter Injection provides dependencies after the object has been created.

It is useful when a dependency is optional or may change later.

**Important Annotations**
@SpringBootApplication

Starts the Spring Boot application and enables auto-configuration and component scanning.

@RestController

Marks a class as a REST Controller that handles HTTP requests.

@Service

Marks a class that contains business logic.

@Repository

Marks a class responsible for database operations.
